.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt DTRACE_PF 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtrace_pf
.Nd a DTrace provider for the pf packet filter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Li pf:ip:test:entry,finish
.Pp
.Li pf:ip:rules:entry
.br
.Li pf:ip:anchor:enter
.br
.Li pf:ip:limiter:decision,pressure,eligible
.Pp
.Li pf::reason:set
.Pp
.Li pf:state:state:create,insert,transition,remove,free
.br
.Li pf:state:purge:run
.Pp
.Li pf:frag:reassemble,reassemble6:entry
.br
.Li pf:nat:transaddr:entry
.br
.Li pf:nat:af_to:translate
.br
.Li pf:ip,ip6:route_to:entry
.Pp
.Li pf:eth:test_rule:entry,test,mismatch,match,final_match
.br
.Li pf:eth:dummynet:submit,reinject
.br
.Li pf:eth:bridge_to:transmit
.br
.Li pf:eth:hook:link
.Pp
.Li pf:table:addr:match,update
.br
.Li pf:rule:jail:match,resolve
.br
.Li pf:syncookie:cookie:send,validate
.Pp
.Li pf:log:pflog:packet
.br
.Li pf:pfsync:packet:send,input
.br
.Li pf:pflow:flow:export
.br
.Li pf:queue:packet:delay
.Pp
.Li pf:ioctl:ioctl:entry,return
.br
.Li pf:ioctl:xact:begin,commit,rollback
.Pp
.Li sdt:::pf-table-begin,pf-table-commit,pf-table-rollback
.br
.Li sdt:::pf-syncookie-active
.br
.Li sdt:::pfsync-queue-pressure
.br
.Li sdt:::pfsync-bulk-start,pfsync-bulk-status-send
.br
.Li sdt:::pfsync-bulk-retry,pfsync-bulk-failed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm pf
provider instruments
.Xr pf 4 ,
the
.Ox
packet filter.
All probes are statically defined
.Pq Xr SDT 9
and cost nothing when not enabled.
Structure arguments use the types of the
.Ox
.In net/pfvar.h
and are available to D scripts through CTF.
.Ss Packet path
.Bl -tag -width "pf::reason:set"
.It Li pf:ip:test:entry
Fires before
.Fn pf_test
for a packet.
.Fa arg0
is the address family,
.Fa arg1
the direction (1 in, 2 out, 3 forwarded) and
.Fa args[2]
the
.Vt struct ifnet .
.It Li pf:ip:test:finish
Fires after
.Fn pf_test
with
.Fa arg0
the action (0 pass, 1 drop),
.Fa arg1
the direction and
.Fa args[2]
the interface.
.It Li pf:ip:rules:entry
Ruleset evaluation of a packet without matching state;
.Fa args[0]
is the
.Vt struct pf_pdesc .
.It Li pf:ip:anchor:enter
A ruleset (the main ruleset or an anchor) is evaluated;
.Fa args[1]
is the
.Vt struct pf_ruleset .
.It Li pf::reason:set
Every point where pf records a reason code
.Pq Dv PFRES_*
for a drop, a match or a normalisation decision.
.Fa arg0
is the reason,
.Fa arg1
the source file and
.Fa arg2
the line.
The reasons are: 0 match, 1 bad-offset, 2 fragment, 3 short, 4
normalize, 5 memory, 6 bad-timestamp, 7 congestion, 8 ip-option, 9
proto-cksum, 10 state-mismatch, 11 state-insert, 12 state-limit, 13
src-limit, 14 synproxy, 15 translate, 16 no-route.
.It Li pf:frag:reassemble:entry,Li pf:frag:reassemble6:entry
An IPv4 or IPv6 fragment enters reassembly;
.Fa args[0]
is the mbuf and
.Fa arg1
the direction.
.It Li pf:nat:transaddr:entry
A nat-to, rdr-to or binat-to address is selected;
.Fa args[0]
is the rule,
.Fa args[1]
the packet description.
.It Li pf:nat:af_to:translate
A packet is translated between address families (af-to).
.It Li pf:ip:route_to:entry,Li pf:ip6:route_to:entry
route-to, reply-to or dup-to routing of a packet;
.Fa args[1]
is the state.
.El
.Ss Ethernet rules
These probes cover the 5BSD
.Ic ether
rules
.Pq see Xr pf.conf 5 ,
with the names and arguments of the
.Fx
pf probes.
A rule is a
.Vt struct pf_keth_rule ,
whose first member is the
.Vt struct pf_eth_rule
of
.In net/pfvar.h .
.Bl -tag -width "pf:eth:test_rule:final_match"
.It Li pf:eth:test_rule:entry
A frame is filtered;
.Fa arg0
is the direction (1 in, 2 out),
.Fa args[1]
the interface and
.Fa args[2]
the mbuf.
.It Li pf:eth:test_rule:test
Rule number
.Fa arg0 ,
.Fa args[1] ,
is evaluated.
.It Li pf:eth:test_rule:mismatch
The rule does not match;
.Fa arg2
names the condition that failed:
.Dq kif ,
.Dq dir ,
.Dq proto ,
.Dq src ,
.Dq dst ,
.Dq ip_src ,
.Dq ip_dst
or
.Dq match_tag .
.It Li pf:eth:test_rule:match
The rule matches; evaluation continues unless it is
.Cm quick .
.It Li pf:eth:test_rule:final_match
The rule that decides,
.Fa arg0
-1 and
.Fa args[1]
NULL when no rule matched and the frame passes.
.It Li pf:eth:dummynet:submit
A frame is sent to
.Xr dummynet 4 ;
.Fa args[0]
is the rule,
.Fa arg1
the pipe or queue number and
.Fa arg2
the direction.
.It Li pf:eth:dummynet:reinject
.Xr dummynet 4
passes a shaped frame on;
.Fa arg0
is the direction and
.Fa args[1]
the interface.
.It Li pf:eth:bridge_to:transmit
A frame is sent out of the
.Cm bridge-to
interface
.Fa args[1]
(NULL if it does not exist, and the frame is dropped).
.It Li pf:eth:hook:link
The link-layer
.Xr pfil 9
hooks of the current vnet are linked
.Pq Fa arg0 No 1
or unlinked (0).
.El
.Ss States
.Bl -tag -width "pf:state:state:transition"
.It Li pf:state:state:create
A rule creates a state:
.Fa args[0]
packet description,
.Fa args[1]
rule,
.Fa args[2]
anchor rule.
.It Li pf:state:state:insert
A state is inserted into the state table.
.It Li pf:state:state:transition
A TCP peer changes protocol state:
.Fa args[0]
state,
.Fa arg1
peer (0 source, 1 destination),
.Fa arg2
new state.
.It Li pf:state:state:remove,free
A state is unlinked and later freed.
.It Li pf:state:purge:run
A purge pass of expired states with
.Fa arg0
the scan limit.
.El
.Ss Packet delay
.Bl -tag -width "pf:queue:packet:delay"
.It Li pf:queue:packet:delay
A packet has obtained delay storage and is about to be scheduled:
.Fa arg0
is the queue ID,
.Fa arg1
the requested delay in milliseconds, and
.Fa arg2
the interface index.
The probe exposes packet metadata independently of its storage layout.
Its availability does not imply that the native output path supports
.Cm set delay .
.El
.Ss Tables, logging, synchronisation and control
.Bl -tag -width "pf:table:addr:update"
.It Li pf:table:addr:match
An address is looked up in table
.Fa args[0]
.Pq Vt struct pfr_ktable .
.It Li pf:table:addr:update
Table statistics are updated for a packet.
.It Li pf:rule:jail:match
The 5BSD
.Cm jail
rule option of rule
.Fa args[0]
.Pq Vt struct pf_rule
matched a socket of jail ID
.Fa arg1 .
.It Li pf:rule:jail:resolve
Rule
.Fa args[0]
names a jail and was re-resolved after a jail was created, renamed or
removed:
.Fa arg1
is the old jail ID and
.Fa arg2
the new one, -2 for no jail.
.It Li pf:syncookie:cookie:send,validate
A SYN cookie is sent or an ACK is validated against one.
.It Li pf:log:pflog:packet
A packet is logged to a
.Xr pflog 4
interface:
.Fa args[0]
packet description,
.Fa arg1
reason,
.Fa args[2]
matching rule,
.Fa args[3]
anchor rule.
.It Li pf:pfsync:packet:send,input
A
.Xr pfsync 4
packet is sent or received.
.It Li pf:pflow:flow:export
A state is exported as a
.Xr pflow 4
flow record.
.It Li pf:ioctl:ioctl:entry,return
A
.Pa /dev/pf
ioctl:
.Fa arg0
command,
.Fa arg1
per-open unit and, on return,
.Fa arg2
the error.
.It Li pf:ioctl:xact:begin,commit,rollback
A ruleset transaction step for the named anchor.
.El
.Ss State and source limiters
These probes fire in rule evaluation for rules that use a state or source
limiter.
.Fa arg0
is the limiter kind (0 state, 1 source) and
.Fa arg1
its identifier.
.Bl -tag -width "pf:ip:limiter:decision"
.It Li pf:ip:limiter:decision
A limiter stops the rule from creating state:
.Fa arg2
rule number,
.Fa arg3
reason (0 missing limiter, 1 hard limit, 2 rate limit,
3 source-address entry capacity),
.Fa arg4
configured action and
.Fa arg5
1 if the packet is blocked, 0 if evaluation falls through to the next rule.
A missing limiter always falls through.
.It Li pf:ip:limiter:pressure
The values behind a hard, rate or capacity rejection:
.Fa arg2
reason,
.Fa arg3
observed value (states, elapsed nanoseconds or source entries),
.Fa arg4
threshold and
.Fa arg5
configured action.
.It Li pf:ip:limiter:eligible
The limiter checks passed for rule
.Fa arg2 .
This is not packet admission: later checks can still reject the packet.
.El
.Ss Function-boundary contracts
These
.Li sdt
provider probes carry scalar arguments only.
.Bl -tag -width "pfsync-bulk-status-send"
.It Li pf-table-begin , pf-table-rollback
A table transaction began or was rolled back:
.Fa arg0
flags,
.Fa arg1
affected inactive tables,
.Fa arg2
0.
.It Li pf-table-commit
A table transaction commit:
.Fa arg0
flags,
.Fa arg1
added and changed tables,
.Fa arg2
0 or
.Er EBUSY
for an invalid or closed ticket.
.It Li pf-syncookie-active
SYN cookies were switched on or off:
.Fa arg0
active,
.Fa arg1
configured mode.
.It Li pfsync-queue-pressure
A
.Xr pfsync 4
slice must send its packet before queueing more:
.Fa arg0
slice,
.Fa arg1
bytes queued,
.Fa arg2
bytes requested.
.It Li pfsync-bulk-start
A bulk update send began for softc
.Fa arg0 .
.It Li pfsync-bulk-status-send
A bulk update status message
.Pq Dv PFSYNC_BUS_*
.Fa arg1
is about to be sent.
This is an attempt, not confirmed delivery.
.It Li pfsync-bulk-retry , pfsync-bulk-failed
A bulk update request timed out:
.Fa arg0
is the attempt count; failed means no further retry.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/share/bsdinstruments/profiles/pf-*.d" -compact
.It Pa /usr/share/dtrace/pf-observe
summary of verdicts, latency, reasons, states, NAT, tables, pflog,
pfsync and pflow activity
.It Pa /usr/share/bsdinstruments/profiles/pf-*.d
focused profiles: pf-latency, pf-audit, pf-drops, pf-states,
pf-frags, pf-nat, pf-tables, pf-rules, pf-pfsync, pf-queues,
pf-limiter-decisions, pf-table-cookie-events, pfsync-recovery-events
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Count drops by reason and source location:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# dtrace -n 'pf::reason:set { @[arg0, stringof(arg1), arg2] = count(); }'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr pflog 4 ,
.Xr pflow 4 ,
.Xr pfsync 4 ,
.Xr pfctl 8 ,
.Xr SDT 9
